is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: web_server_0
diagnosis_text:
The issue is not DNS or general reachability. From host_1_1_1_1, web0.local resolves to 10.200.0.3 (getent hosts). HTTP works and returns 200 OK quickly (curl http://web0.local and http://10.200.0.3 both succeed). The failure is specific to HTTPS: curl -k https://web0.local and https://10.200.0.3 return 000 immediately, indicating no TLS service. On web_server_0, Apache is running and listening only on 0.0.0.0:80 (ss/netstat), and there is no listener on 443. Apache’s config shows only a :80 VirtualHost (apachectl -S) and no SSL modules loaded (apachectl -M shows neither ssl nor gnutls). Although ports.conf contains conditional “Listen 443,” it is inactive because the SSL module is not enabled.

Mechanism: clie
